---
title: ResBack - Component Diagram
config:
    flowchart:
        wrappingWidth: 380
        nodeSpacing: 45
        rankSpacing: 60
---
flowchart TB
    subgraph CLIENT["Client / web browser"]
        UI["«component» Web UI<br/>HTML / CSS / JavaScript<br/>Chart.js, forms, AJAX pagination"]
    end

    subgraph APP["ResBack / Laravel application - single deployable"]
        WEB["«component» Web interface<br/>Web routes, access middleware<br/>Blade page and partial rendering"]

        ACCOUNTS["«component» Identity and accounts<br/>Login / registration / role navigation<br/>Account administration / profiles"]
        FEEDBACK["«component» Feedback management<br/>Submission, history and deletion<br/>FeedbackController"]
        REPORTS["«component» Dashboard and reporting<br/>Dashboard / PDF / Excel controllers<br/>Date and language filters"]

        GUARD["«component» Submission protection<br/>StoreFeedbackRequest<br/>SubmissionGuard / AutoRejectService"]
        ANALYSIS["«component» Sentiment and classification<br/>SentimentService<br/>LanguageCategoryService / ConcernTopicService"]
        RANKING["«component» Concern ranking<br/>ConcernRankingService<br/>Current scores / persisted ranking rebuilds"]
        EXPORT["«library» Document generation<br/>Dompdf - PDF<br/>PhpSpreadsheet - XLSX"]

        DATA["«component» Data access<br/>Laravel Eloquent models<br/>User / Category / Feedback<br/>SentimentResult / ConcernRanking"]
        STATE["«framework component» Session and cache support<br/>Laravel Auth sessions / RateLimiter<br/>Configurable storage drivers"]
    end

    DB[("«datastore» Relational database<br/>MySQL / MariaDB or SQLite<br/>Application records")]
    FILES[("«datastore» Public file storage<br/>Uploaded profile photos<br/>Laravel public disk")]
    GEMINI["«external service» Google Gemini API<br/>Gemma feedback analysis<br/>HTTPS / JSON"]

    UI -. "HTTP forms and AJAX" .-> WEB
    WEB -. "account and profile routes" .-> ACCOUNTS
    WEB -. "feedback routes" .-> FEEDBACK
    WEB -. "dashboard and export routes" .-> REPORTS
    WEB -. "authenticated sessions" .-> STATE

    ACCOUNTS -. "accounts and roles" .-> DATA
    ACCOUNTS -. "login and logout" .-> STATE
    ACCOUNTS -. "store or remove photo" .-> FILES

    FEEDBACK -. "validate and check" .-> GUARD
    FEEDBACK -. "accepted feedback only" .-> ANALYSIS
    FEEDBACK -. "save, read or delete" .-> DATA
    GUARD -. "duplicate checks" .-> DATA
    GUARD -. "rate limits" .-> STATE

    ANALYSIS -. "synchronous API request" .-> GEMINI
    ANALYSIS -. "save result and status" .-> DATA
    ANALYSIS -. "rebuild category rankings" .-> RANKING

    REPORTS -. "query feedback and analysis" .-> DATA
    REPORTS -. "calculate current rankings" .-> RANKING
    REPORTS -. "generate downloads" .-> EXPORT
    RANKING -. "read analysis; persist rebuilds" .-> DATA
    DATA -. "SQL via configured connection" .-> DB

    classDef component fill:#f8fafc,stroke:#64748b,color:#172b4d;
    classDef external fill:#eef5fb,stroke:#52789b,color:#172b4d;
    class UI,WEB,ACCOUNTS,FEEDBACK,REPORTS,GUARD,ANALYSIS,RANKING,EXPORT,DATA,STATE component;
    class DB,FILES,GEMINI external;
    style CLIENT fill:#ffffff,stroke:#94a3b8,color:#172b4d
    style APP fill:#ffffff,stroke:#94a3b8,color:#172b4d

%% UML-style logical component view, expressed with Mermaid flowchart syntax.
%% Component boxes group collaborating implementation classes; they are not
%% separate deployable services. Arrows point from consumer to dependency.
%% Responses return along the same requests and are not separately drawn.
%% Web interface groups routing, middleware and server-side Blade rendering;
%% browser Web UI runs the resulting HTML/CSS/JS, not Blade itself.
%% Identity/accounts maps to LoginController, RegisterController, HomeController,
%% AccountController and ProfileController. Protection maps to StoreFeedbackRequest,
%% FeedbackSubmissionGuard and FeedbackAutoRejectService (shortened inside box).
%% Dashboard/reporting maps to DashboardController, FeedbackReportController,
%% FeedbackExportController and FeedbackDateRange. Only dashboard/PDF use ranking;
%% only PDF/Excel use document libraries. Normalization helpers live with analysis;
%% reporting also reads LanguageCategoryService::CATEGORY_LABELS (detail omitted).
%% Request validation precedes controller execution. Rejected feedback is stored,
%% bypasses external analysis, and is excluded from faculty reports.
%% Gemini analysis is synchronous; no queue worker or message broker is implied.
%% Rankings are computed on demand for dashboard/PDF. rebuildCategory persists them.
%% Session/cache backing stores vary by configuration; default configuration uses
%% database drivers. A separate database arrow is omitted to avoid implying that
%% every deployment uses the database for this state. Public disk is local by default.
%% DB alternatives describe supported configuration, not a verified active engine.
%% Return HTML/JSON/downloads, build tools, vendor internals, console maintenance,
%% static-file serving, logging, and the /api/user route closure are omitted.
%% Source: routes/web.php, bootstrap/app.php, app/Http, app/Services, app/Models,
%% app/Support, resources/views, resources/js/app.js, config and composer.json.
